  "summary": "The South Fork Landscape review path was still Unlit and its pale source response washed the canyon toward white. The runnable Chili Bar-to-Folsom map used a different parent material and therefore would not have received a review-only fix. V1 now shares one three-scale, slope-aware dry-grass/oak-litter/granitic-soil/weathered-granite response between both paths, with a stronger 0.58 palette correction in the Landscape candidate and a source-preserving 0.30 response in the runnable full reach. Fixed-camera evidence is materially less washed out and the playable reach now reads as a summer Sierra foothill corridor, but coarse terrain, synthetic vegetation, sparse mid-story cover, smooth water, and lighting still fail photoreal acceptance.",
